TI  - Rethinking Subjective Trust in LLM: Actualizing Tangibility from Uncertainty
AB  - Large language models (LLMs) are increasingly used in high-stakes domains, raising concerns about how users can reliably trust them. Existing evaluations focus mostly on model-centric trustworthiness, overlooking the dynamic and user-involved nature of trust. We break down the subjective trust into dimensions of perceptibility, openness, progressiveness, robustness, and uncertainty. We further propose a five-level evaluation structure that measures these dimensions. Our analysis highlights domain-specific trust requirements and provides guidance for designing models that support calibrated and resilient user trust.
