TI  - Enhancing access to justice through chatbot technology: on the effectiveness of artificial intelligence in the delivery of legal advice
AB  - Many people are interested in how effectively robots and AI can enhance access to justice.This study examines Kazakhstan's digital court system and explores how large language models (LLMs) and question-answering (QA) tools can improve the quality, usability, and efficiency of legal services.The models -LLaMA-3B, GEMMA-9B, Phi-14B, Qwen-7B, and Mistral-7B -were trained and tested using data from leading Kazakh legal websites such as Adilet, Zqai, and Gov.kz, evaluated through ROUGE, METEOR, and expert review metrics.Among them, GPT-4o-mini achieved the highest accuracy and usability scores, demonstrating strong proficiency in the Kazakh language.The findings show that, in our study sample, AI-driven chatbots inspire more user trust than rule-based systems, indicating potential for boosting public confidence in digital judicial services.Overall, the study shows that LLM-powered legal advisory systems have the potential to advance sustainability, equity, and accessibility in national legal systems, which calls for further extensive research.
